(Byte strings in STEF support a rich variety of decorative notations.
All non-hex characters between hex pairs are ignored by parsers, making
it natural to express binary data in whatever form fits the domain.)


(--- The same four bytes, written eight different ways ---)

(Compact: no separators)
'DEADBEEF'

(Space-separated: hex dump style)
'DE AD BE EF'

(0x-prefixed: Python and C literal style)
'0xDE 0xAD 0xBE 0xEF'

(\x-prefixed: C string escape style)
'\xDE\xAD\xBE\xEF'

(Colon-separated: MAC address and TLS fingerprint style)
'DE:AD:BE:EF'

(Dot-separated: certificate serial number style)
'DE.AD.BE.EF'

(Hash-prefixed: CSS web colour style)
'#DEADBEEF'

(Bracketed: structured grouping style)
'[DE][AD][BE][EF]'


(--- Real-world examples ---)

(SHA-256 digest of the empty string, compact)
'e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855'

(Same digest, split into 8-byte groups for readability)
'e3b0c442 98fc1c14 9afbf4c8 996fb924 27ae41e4 649b934c a495991b 7852b855'

(128-bit AES-128 key in \x notation)
'\x00\x11\x22\x33\x44\x55\x66\x77\x88\x99\xAA\xBB\xCC\xDD\xEE\xFF'

(Ethernet MAC address, colon-separated)
'2C:54:91:88:C9:E3'

(IPv4 address 192.168.1.1 as four raw bytes, dot-separated)
'C0.A8.01.01'

(IPv6 address as sixteen raw bytes, grouped like standard IPv6 notation)
'2001:0DB8:0000:0000:0000:0000:0000:0001'

(RGBA colour using CSS hash-prefix notation)
'#FF5733FF'

(UUID as raw bytes, grouped by UUID field widths)
'550E8400-E29B-41D4-A716-446655440000'

(x86 instruction: PUSH RBP / MOV RBP,RSP / XORL EAX,EAX)
'55 48 89 E5 31 C0'

(PNG magic bytes in block form)
'''
89 50 4E 47 0D 0A 1A 0A
'''

(Public key DER header and first few bytes of modulus, multi-line block)
'''
30 82 01 22 30 0D 06 09  2A 86 48 86 F7 0D 01 01
01 05 00 03 82 01 0F 00  30 82 01 0A 02 82 01 01
00 B3 51 0A 09 F2 35 C9  A5 C2 28 C5 FF 50 A4 2B
'''


